body:
Has there been any progress on this? I am working on a project that requires me to render models from a D3D9 game that use custom src and dest blend modes. I personally like the added shader keyword approach, but I also feel it might be better to split it into 2 separate keywords, `src_blend` and `dest_blend`, and specify `blend_custom` for `render_mode`. ie:

```glsl
shader_type spatial;
render_mode blend_custom;
src_blend src_alpha;
dest_blend inv_src_alpha;
```

This would simplify the parsing of custom blend modes and material -> shader code generation.
